    "result_text": "Done. The build is green \u2014 both acceptance tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe identity key was previously a plain pipe-delimited string `telephone|email|householdId`. I redesigned it per the spec and cascaded the consequences through duplicate detection and soft-matching.\n\n**`mapper/IdentityKeyResolver.java`** \u2014 `deriveIdentityKey` now returns the full 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`. The `householdId` is no longer part of the key.\n\n**`mapper/SoundexResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a static utility computing standard American Soundex, used by both the identity key and the soft-match. Implemented in-repo rather than depending on commons-codec (not a declared dependency).\n\n**`mapper/HexDigest.java`** \u2014 added `lowerHex(...)` for the full lowercase digest (the existing helper only produced an uppercase prefix).\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `isPossibleDuplicateOf` (soft-match) now fires when `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match but the `identityKey` differs (instead of the old exact-lastName + different-telephone rule). Since telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones now have different keys \u2192 they're created as a soft match rather than rejected. Removed the now-unused `java.util.Objects` import.\n\n**`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 the 409 duplicate response now reports the fields `telephone, email, lastName` (was `householdId`).\n\n## Behavioural outcome, matching the spec\n- **409 duplicate detection** is now the single identity key \u2014 still ignoring soft-deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (during `normalizeAndValidate`, before the key is derived).\n- The **separate household-duplicate 409** no longer exists \u2014 `householdId` is out of the key. `householdId` is still computed and used for membership-level capping and household member counts.\n- Same lastName + postcode, **different telephone** \u2192 soft match (created), not a 409.\n\nI also updated the surrounding Javadoc that described the old key composition so the docs stay accurate.",
